   "id": "rule-only-your-own-software-hardware-and-builds-or-a-clients-with-written-author",
   "name": "Only your own software, hardware and builds, or a client's with written authorisation",
   "kind": "rule",
   "category": "Reverse engineering",
   "url": null,
   "description": "Only your own software, hardware and builds, or a client's with written authorisation. Canada's Copyright Act s.41.12 allows getting around a technological protection measure on a LAWFULLY OBTAINED program only to achieve interoperability, and the exemption is lost if it is used to infringe. App/game terms of service often forbid reverse engineering even where the law allows it.",
   "verdict": null,
   "verdictNote": null,
   "why": "Run RE tools only in an isolated VM, never on a production server or a machine holding API keys; never add a reverse-engineered private API to the public API catalogue; keep a one-line written purpose for each RE job; not legal advice: ask a lawyer before any client RE engagement.",
